EXTRA["beep-test-calculator"] += [
    s("Comparing with past results",
      "When you compare two tests, look at the conditions first. A higher score on a cool evening after a rest day and a lower score on a hot afternoon after a match don't necessarily mean fitness has fallen. Note the time of day, surface, temperature, footwear and what training you did in the previous two days. Over several tests, those notes make the trend clear and stop one unusual result from changing the plan."),
]
EXTRA["cooper-test-calculator"] += [
    s("Comparing with past results",
      "When you compare two Cooper tests, check that the course, lane, weather and preparation were similar. A 100 m difference can come from wind or a hot day as easily as from fitness. Keep notes on conditions and how you paced each test, so a real improvement stands out from day-to-day variation. If two tests in a row show a fall in distance under similar conditions, review recovery, sleep and training load with your coach."),
]
EXTRA["vo2-max-calculator"] += [
    s("Comparing with past results",
      "Compare estimates only from the same method. A Cooper result and a heart rate estimate can differ by ten points without any change in fitness. Keep a simple log with the date, method, result and conditions. Over a year, a rising line in the same test is the clearest sign that training is working, and a flat line is a useful prompt to adjust the plan with your coach."),
]
